    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `timezone` field is a derived, read-only property on the owner \u2014 consistent with how `locality` and the other computed fields already work in this codebase (a `@Transient` getter on the `Owner` entity, serialized out through the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` via MapStruct's name-based mapping).\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`**\n   - Added a fixed `REGION_TIMEZONE` lookup table: `NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`.\n   - Added `@Transient public String getTimezone()`, which maps the owner's `getLocality()` (its region) through that table, returning `null` for any region not listed (e.g. `UNKNOWN`).\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n   - Added the read-only `timezone` string field to the owner schema (right after `locality`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and the mapper populates it automatically.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` now passes: a Sydney owner (postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW) returns `locality: \"NSW\"` and `timezone: \"Australia/Sydney\"`.",
