    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the existing structure cleanly:\n\n- `REGION_TIMEZONE` is placed alongside the sibling lookup tables (`CITY_REGION`, `REGION_POSTCODE_RANGES`), follows their exact `Map.of(...)` shape, and carries a doc comment in the same style noting the \"not listed\" fallback.\n- `getTimezone()` mirrors the other derived, `@Transient` getters (`getLocality()`, `getContactPreference()`, `getIdentityKey()`): a one-liner that composes on `getLocality()` rather than re-deriving the region, so there's no duplication of the region-resolution logic. Logic lives in the right unit \u2014 a derived field on `Owner` next to its peers.\n- Returning `null` for unmapped regions via `Map.get` is consistent with the codebase's use of `null`/`\"UNKNOWN\"` sentinels, and the Javadoc documents it.\n- The `openapi.yml` entry matches the formatting, ordering, and `readOnly`/`example`/`description` conventions of the adjacent `locality` and `contactPreference` properties.\n\nNothing is becoming a catch-all and a maintainer here would find it natural.",
